    "reason": "Over the 30 days, A returned ROAS 4.0 ($200 revenue on $50 spend per day, $25 CPA) against B's 1.8. It is stable and has been running since 2025-01, so a scale-up is low risk. I capped the increase at +20% so the delivery system isn't pushed back into learning. Note that both campaigns show a 'shared' budget of 100, and their combined spend is exactly 100/day. That suggests they draw from one pool, so you can't set per-campaign amounts until you split it into campaign-level budgets (A 120, B 80). If you keep the shared budget, the only lever is the total, and you'd leave it at 100 or raise it modestly."
